Here's how to handle each scenario:

### 1. Platform-specific (Windows only)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]          // Microsoft.AspNetCore.Testing
// or roll your own:
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("WindowsOnly")]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows.");
    // ...
}
```

### 2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU)

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void Render_UsesGpu()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") is not null)
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI – requires local GPU.");
    // ...
}
```

Or create a reusable attribute:

```csharp
[AttributeUsage(AttributeTargets.Method)]
public class SkipInCIAttribute : Attribute, ITestDataSource
{ /* return empty data when CI env var is set */ }
```

### 3. Flaky external API — retry with `[TestCategory]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Flaky")]
[Timeout(30_000)]
public async Task Weather_ReturnsForecast()
{
    Exception? last = null;
    for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
    {
        try
        {
            var result = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync();
            Assert.IsNotNull(result);
            return; // success
        }
        catch (HttpRequestException ex) { last = ex; }
        await Task.Delay(1000 * (i + 1)); // back-off
    }
    Assert.Fail($"Failed after 3 retries: {last?.Message}");
}
```

Filter flaky tests out of your main run:

```bash
dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=Flaky"
```

### 4. Cleanup even on failure — use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public class TempFileTests
{
    private string? _tempFile;

    [TestInitialize]
    public void Setup()
        => _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();

    [TestCleanup]                         // runs even if the test fails
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        if (_tempFile is not null && File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void WriteAndRead_RoundTrips()
    {
        File.WriteAllText(_tempFile!, "hello");
        Assert.AreEqual("hello", File.ReadAllText(_tempFile!));
    }
}
```

### Quick reference

| Scenario | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| OS-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` / guard check |
| Skip in CI | Check `CI` env var, `Assert.Inconclusive()` |
| Flaky test | Retry loop + `[TestCategory("Flaky")]` to filter |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` (instance) or `[ClassCleanup]` (shared) |

`Assert.Inconclusive()` marks the test as **skipped/warning** rather than failed, so it won't break your pipeline.
